1
00:00:14,815 --> 00:00:17,015
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

2
00:00:36,425 --> 00:00:38,086
Welcome to Sunny Mart. How may I help you?

3
00:02:18,426 --> 00:02:22,426
Help...help me!

4
00:03:35,809 --> 00:03:36,856
Which one do you want, Nava?

5
00:03:53,945 --> 00:03:54,594
Got it.

6
00:03:57,648 --> 00:03:59,382
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

7
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:05,312
Excuse me.

8
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:07,449
Could you please get in line?

9
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:08,785
I’ll just pay real quick.

10
00:04:12,991 --> 00:04:13,671
Fine, whatever.

11
00:04:20,812 --> 00:04:22,734
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

12
00:04:27,218 --> 00:04:28,663
You’re off to school early today.

13
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,304
I don't need the bag.

14
00:04:34,632 --> 00:04:36,296
Oh, aren’t you going to work today?

15
00:04:41,921 --> 00:04:44,663
Would you like some shumai or steamed buns? They’re half price right now.

16
00:05:02,249 --> 00:05:04,421
Are you excited to be starting elementary school, Nava?

17
00:05:09,890 --> 00:05:12,491
I’ll put this doll in your bag, so it can keep you company.

18
00:05:19,413 --> 00:05:20,398
Remember to say hello to your teacher, dear.

19
00:05:43,757 --> 00:05:44,347
Metha?

20
00:05:46,616 --> 00:05:47,913
You really are here.

21
00:05:52,702 --> 00:05:53,778
I thought you said you’d quit.

22
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:05,187
I saw a clip of you yesterday.

23
00:06:09,765 --> 00:06:10,695
You’re getting famous now, huh?

24
00:06:21,755 --> 00:06:23,161
The guy was smoking where smoking’s prohibited.

25
00:06:24,263 --> 00:06:25,528
There was even a sign.

26
00:06:27,427 --> 00:06:28,739
I get that you meant well.

27
00:06:30,083 --> 00:06:32,466
But don’t you think you went a bit overboard?

28
00:06:33,466 --> 00:06:34,606
You got him fired, man.

29
00:06:36,552 --> 00:06:38,372
He wouldn't if he’d followed the rules in the first place.

30
00:06:40,388 --> 00:06:42,849
If it were that simple, why would we even need the police?

31
00:06:46,356 --> 00:06:46,981
See you around.

32
00:06:47,931 --> 00:06:48,485
Hey.

33
00:06:51,419 --> 00:06:52,426
Seriously.

34
00:06:54,310 --> 00:06:56,020
don’t you ever think about becoming a cop again?

35
00:07:01,770 --> 00:07:03,263
I wouldn’t be able to change anything anyway.

36
00:07:08,731 --> 00:07:09,544
Come on, man.

37
00:07:10,247 --> 00:07:12,661
But at least you’d still make a living, right?

38
00:07:58,802 --> 00:08:00,123
Amazing!

39
00:08:00,527 --> 00:08:01,293
Yeah!

40
00:08:02,316 --> 00:08:03,139
Yeah!

41
00:08:03,164 --> 00:08:04,483
Daddy, you’re amazing!

42
00:08:04,508 --> 00:08:06,772
You’re Super Dad. You can do anything!

43
00:08:06,829 --> 00:08:07,778
If there’s a Super Dad,

44
00:08:07,802 --> 00:08:10,835
then there must be a Super Nava, too!

45
00:08:12,579 --> 00:08:13,477
Super Nava!

46
00:09:11,524 --> 00:09:13,644
(Drop by Sunny, Happy Every Day.)

47
00:09:14,789 --> 00:09:17,399
Hello. Welcome to Sunny Mart!

48
00:09:24,793 --> 00:09:29,966
(Urgently hiring night shift staff!)

49
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:39,679
Ten thousand a night, not a month?

50
00:09:48,751 --> 00:09:49,605
Yes.

51
00:09:50,366 --> 00:09:54,304
The night-shift staff get paid 10,000 baht per night.

52
00:09:55,093 --> 00:09:56,221
That’s correct.

53
00:09:57,034 --> 00:10:00,348
And the best part is, we pay you daily.

54
00:10:00,704 --> 00:10:03,961
As soon as you finish your shift, you get paid.

55
00:10:07,758 --> 00:10:09,267
The job must be really tough, right?

56
00:10:09,345 --> 00:10:11,303
No, it's not.

57
00:10:11,327 --> 00:10:13,963
It’s just like working at any other convenience store.

58
00:10:14,416 --> 00:10:17,492
You just have to follow all the employee rules.

59
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:22,843
Just follow the rules?

60
00:10:25,456 --> 00:10:28,541
If you’re interested, come apply.

61
00:10:28,565 --> 00:10:30,729
We’re urgently hiring right now.

62
00:10:34,685 --> 00:10:35,735
Ten thousand a night.

63
00:10:38,073 --> 00:10:39,058
I’ll think about it.

64
00:10:40,602 --> 00:10:42,043
All right. See you.

65
00:11:10,357 --> 00:11:11,744
Mr. Metha.

66
00:11:12,886 --> 00:11:14,533
Ever since you borrowed money,

67
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:16,490
you’ve been awfully hard to get ahold of.

68
00:11:17,779 --> 00:11:18,518
Sir.

69
00:11:19,995 --> 00:11:21,018
I was just about to call you.

70
00:11:23,315 --> 00:11:24,292
But you know

71
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:27,604
you’re already two days late paying me back, right?

72
00:11:30,642 --> 00:11:32,366
I’ll find a way to pay you back.

73
00:11:35,003 --> 00:11:36,171
Mr. Metha.

74
00:11:37,417 --> 00:11:41,212
I’ve been lending money for over 10 years.

75
00:11:41,767 --> 00:11:42,863
You know what?

76
00:11:43,673 --> 00:11:48,734
People who are desperate all act exactly like you do.

77
00:11:49,774 --> 00:11:50,607
Hey.

78
00:11:58,068 --> 00:11:59,261
Metha!

79
00:12:00,071 --> 00:12:00,829
Go after him!

80
00:12:05,393 --> 00:12:06,583
You’re pretty good at running away, huh?

81
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:08,028
You think I wouldn’t catch up with you?

82
00:12:09,525 --> 00:12:10,282
The lighter.

83
00:12:26,750 --> 00:12:28,453
Why did you think you could get away from me?

84
00:12:29,801 --> 00:12:30,308
Huh?

85
00:12:31,108 --> 00:12:31,833
Huh?

86
00:12:34,827 --> 00:12:35,461
Tomorrow.

87
00:12:36,917 --> 00:12:38,075
I’ll get the money for you tomorrow.

88
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:39,936
I swear.

89
00:12:41,765 --> 00:12:42,554
Sure.

90
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:44,968
I’m a man who gives people chances.

91
00:12:50,056 --> 00:12:52,264
But if you can’t pay tomorrow,

92
00:12:53,194 --> 00:12:55,904
it won't just end here.

93
00:12:57,246 --> 00:12:58,105
Got it?

94
00:13:01,659 --> 00:13:02,698
Right.

95
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:05,864
This motorcycle.

96
00:13:06,472 --> 00:13:07,709
I’ll take it as interest on the debt.

97
00:13:48,744 --> 00:13:53,430
(Urgently hiring night shift staff!)

98
00:14:18,086 --> 00:14:18,918
Here.

99
00:14:21,184 --> 00:14:25,159
Metha Triwikul. Goes by Metha.

100
00:14:25,613 --> 00:14:26,635
Age 34.

101
00:14:30,495 --> 00:14:31,380
Okay.

102
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:33,162
You meet all the requirements.

103
00:14:34,051 --> 00:14:35,460
You can start tonight.

104
00:14:39,518 --> 00:14:41,584
Wait, I got the job already?

105
00:14:41,994 --> 00:14:42,501
That’s right.

106
00:14:43,296 --> 00:14:46,309
We’re short-staffed on the night shift right now.

107
00:14:46,633 --> 00:14:50,378
If you can start right away, we’d like you to start tonight.

108
00:14:52,927 --> 00:14:54,826
Is anything stopping you?

109
00:14:55,097 --> 00:14:56,441
Oh, no problem at all.

110
00:14:57,321 --> 00:14:58,612
I can start tonight.

111
00:14:58,804 --> 00:15:00,228
Great.

112
00:15:00,645 --> 00:15:03,149
Our night-shift staff start at midnight.

113
00:15:03,174 --> 00:15:05,918
I’d like you to arrive ten minutes

114
00:15:05,942 --> 00:15:06,828
before your shift begins.

115
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,664
That’s the first rule

116
00:15:08,968 --> 00:15:10,218
for night-shift employees.

117
00:15:10,916 --> 00:15:12,276
Make sure you remember it.

118
00:15:16,352 --> 00:15:16,923
Thank you.

119
00:15:30,892 --> 00:15:31,739
Nava.

120
00:15:33,474 --> 00:15:35,080
I might not be home with you tonight.

121
00:15:47,227 --> 00:15:48,523
Hello!

122
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:56,273
Hello.

123
00:15:57,116 --> 00:16:00,454
I came right over as soon as you called.

124
00:16:00,892 --> 00:16:03,110
Well, I’ve switched to working nights lately.

125
00:16:04,166 --> 00:16:06,947
Could you look after Nava until 6 am?

126
00:16:08,042 --> 00:16:10,927
Wow, until 6 am?

127
00:16:12,441 --> 00:16:14,671
My back’s been hurting lately.

128
00:16:14,695 --> 00:16:16,447
Sleeping somewhere unfamiliar might...

129
00:16:16,471 --> 00:16:17,241
I’ll pay you.

130
00:16:18,963 --> 00:16:21,321
Oh, we’re practically family!

131
00:16:21,577 --> 00:16:23,257
Just give me 500 baht.

132
00:16:35,587 --> 00:16:37,741
Is 400 baht okay? That’s all I have.

133
00:16:42,298 --> 00:16:43,624
All right, then.

134
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:46,654
Four hundred it is.

135
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:49,437
I’m only charging you that because we’re neighbors.

136
00:16:49,461 --> 00:16:51,406
We’ve got to help each other out.

137
00:16:55,185 --> 00:16:55,980
Nava.

138
00:16:56,758 --> 00:16:58,518
You’ll stay with me today, okay?

139
00:16:59,105 --> 00:17:00,764
I’ll hurry home as soon as my shift ends.

140
00:17:01,430 --> 00:17:02,860
Just hurry up and go.

141
00:17:42,808 --> 00:17:43,758
That scared me.

142
00:17:47,599 --> 00:17:48,591
What is it doing here?

143
00:18:04,514 --> 00:18:05,912
Welcome to Sunny Mart!

144
00:18:18,945 --> 00:18:19,777
Wow.

145
00:18:21,460 --> 00:18:22,758
You look nice.

146
00:18:24,654 --> 00:18:25,580
Here you go.

147
00:18:26,433 --> 00:18:27,937
Your employment contract.

148
00:18:28,790 --> 00:18:30,086
I’ve got everything ready for you.

149
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:33,413
But before you sign, I must advise you

150
00:18:33,690 --> 00:18:37,680
to read every detail of the contract carefully.

151
00:18:37,932 --> 00:18:39,907
This is to protect your own interests.

152
00:18:39,931 --> 00:18:43,569
Especially the 13 rules for night-shift employees.

153
00:18:45,357 --> 00:18:47,290
If you can’t remember them all,

154
00:18:47,314 --> 00:18:49,378
I’ve posted them by the counter.

155
00:18:49,517 --> 00:18:52,781
I recommend memorizing every single one.

156
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:55,232
Because here...

157
00:18:55,824 --> 00:18:56,496
The rules

158
00:18:56,965 --> 00:18:58,634
are a matter of life and death.

159
00:19:01,345 --> 00:19:04,330
If you have any questions, just ask.

160
00:19:09,205 --> 00:19:11,858
Will I really get 10,000 baht per night?

161
00:19:14,384 --> 00:19:15,580
Absolutely.

162
00:19:16,439 --> 00:19:19,048
Don’t worry. It’s right here in the contract.

163
00:19:19,624 --> 00:19:20,697
It's 10,000 baht

164
00:19:21,379 --> 00:19:23,373
as long as you stay for the full shift.

165
00:19:31,736 --> 00:19:32,557
Deal.

166
00:19:41,619 --> 00:19:43,914
Okay, all done.

167
00:19:44,457 --> 00:19:46,958
Let’s take a photo for your employee ID.

168
00:19:47,541 --> 00:19:48,759
Mr. Metha, please wait over there.

169
00:19:52,133 --> 00:19:54,532
Right by that wall. Over there.

170
00:20:05,309 --> 00:20:06,043
Look at the camera.

171
00:20:06,679 --> 00:20:09,139
One, two, three.

172
00:20:19,064 --> 00:20:20,120
Mr. Metha.

173
00:20:22,369 --> 00:20:26,153
Our store has individual lockers for each employee.

174
00:20:26,478 --> 00:20:30,132
You can put your personal belongings in here.

175
00:20:30,157 --> 00:20:32,152
Your mobile phone goes here, too.

176
00:20:34,892 --> 00:20:36,125
Dear’s just arrived.

177
00:20:38,378 --> 00:20:39,060
Dear.

178
00:20:39,844 --> 00:20:43,151
This is Metha, our new night-shift employee.

179
00:20:43,631 --> 00:20:44,916
And this is Dear.

180
00:20:45,321 --> 00:20:48,607
She’s been on the night shift longer than anyone else.

181
00:20:49,028 --> 00:20:51,284
Dear will train you.

182
00:20:51,547 --> 00:20:52,754
No need, Cherd.

183
00:20:53,064 --> 00:20:54,818
Who knows if he’ll even make it through tonight?

184
00:20:56,705 --> 00:20:59,244
Why would you say that, Dear? Look at him first.

185
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:01,252
He looks capable.

186
00:21:01,413 --> 00:21:04,464
He might handle the customers better than we expect.

187
00:21:14,841 --> 00:21:16,857
Rule number 1 for night-shift employees.

188
00:21:17,009 --> 00:21:20,665
You must arrive ten minutes before your shift starts.

189
00:21:25,994 --> 00:21:27,192
It’s only a minute.

190
00:21:28,079 --> 00:21:29,600
I’d still make it on time for work.

191
00:21:29,803 --> 00:21:30,667
You know

192
00:21:31,733 --> 00:21:35,957
how serious the consequences are if you break the rules.

193
00:21:36,135 --> 00:21:38,535
Yes, I know.

194
00:21:39,234 --> 00:21:41,293
So annoying.

195
00:21:43,758 --> 00:21:44,529
Metha.

196
00:21:45,556 --> 00:21:48,558
This is Bird, our other night-shift employee.

197
00:22:42,328 --> 00:22:43,242
Rule number one.

198
00:22:44,028 --> 00:22:47,548
Night-shift working hours are from midnight to six am.

199
00:22:47,958 --> 00:22:49,645
Please arrive 10 minutes early.

200
00:22:50,097 --> 00:22:51,965
You must not leave the convenience store premises

201
00:22:51,989 --> 00:22:53,011
during your shift.

202
00:22:58,675 --> 00:22:59,737
Move. You’re in the way.

203
00:23:08,049 --> 00:23:08,883
Rule number five.

204
00:23:09,465 --> 00:23:11,959
At least one must remain at the counter at all times.

205
00:23:12,596 --> 00:23:13,385
The counter must not be left unattended

206
00:23:13,409 --> 00:23:14,381
for more than three minutes.

207
00:23:24,993 --> 00:23:25,646
Rule number 10.

208
00:23:26,587 --> 00:23:27,693
No expired products

209
00:23:27,717 --> 00:23:29,599
or foreign objects may be left inside the store.

210
00:23:30,232 --> 00:23:31,334
If found, dispose of them.

211
00:23:47,038 --> 00:23:48,554
What should I be doing?

212
00:23:51,841 --> 00:23:53,034
Have you read the rules?

213
00:23:54,225 --> 00:23:56,061
Just follow them. That’s it.

214
00:23:57,232 --> 00:23:59,919
When I started, I learned everything on my own.

215
00:24:06,298 --> 00:24:07,540
How long have you been working here?

216
00:24:09,517 --> 00:24:10,748
Counting today,

217
00:24:11,947 --> 00:24:12,908
exactly seven days.

218
00:24:20,510 --> 00:24:21,909
This hasn’t expired yet, has it?

219
00:24:22,850 --> 00:24:24,178
Shouldn’t we separate it out first?

220
00:24:30,192 --> 00:24:31,122
You trying to teach me how to do my job?

221
00:24:34,483 --> 00:24:35,206
No.

222
00:24:36,124 --> 00:24:38,522
I just thought it’d be easier to check if we separated it.

223
00:24:49,365 --> 00:24:50,943
Don’t tell me how to do my job.

224
00:24:52,962 --> 00:24:54,438
Worry about surviving tonight yourself.

225
00:24:58,342 --> 00:24:59,678
If you’ve got so much free time,

226
00:25:00,303 --> 00:25:02,704
go restock the fridge.

227
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:06,555
Go!

228
00:25:30,858 --> 00:25:32,218
Watermelon tea with dried fish.

229
00:25:32,934 --> 00:25:34,859
Mixed with sticky rice and boba.

230
00:25:38,264 --> 00:25:39,667
Does anyone actually drink this?

231
00:26:28,485 --> 00:26:31,432
(Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart. Please come again!)

232
00:26:38,505 --> 00:26:40,255
What on earth is this?

233
00:26:40,909 --> 00:26:43,810
You can’t even stack a few things without breaking them?

234
00:26:45,891 --> 00:26:47,656
Did a customer come into the store just now?

235
00:27:00,410 --> 00:27:01,354
What did you see?

236
00:27:05,679 --> 00:27:06,239
Nothing.

237
00:27:07,994 --> 00:27:08,900
Must have been my imagination.

238
00:27:12,463 --> 00:27:13,039
No.

239
00:27:14,479 --> 00:27:15,220
Here...

240
00:27:16,287 --> 00:27:17,568
There’s no such thing as “your imagination”

241
00:27:17,592 --> 00:27:18,618
or “seeing things.”

242
00:27:25,054 --> 00:27:25,619
Well...

243
00:27:27,041 --> 00:27:29,192
I think someone was standing in front of the drink fridge.

244
00:27:34,995 --> 00:27:35,661
That’s it?

245
00:27:40,528 --> 00:27:41,541
Rule number one.

246
00:27:43,402 --> 00:27:44,768
Rule number two.

247
00:27:46,853 --> 00:27:48,661
We didn't break any rules.

248
00:27:50,856 --> 00:27:51,768
Better safe than sorry.

249
00:27:54,984 --> 00:27:59,299
Protect me from evil, keep all harm away!

250
00:28:00,767 --> 00:28:01,716
What are you doing?

251
00:28:01,740 --> 00:28:02,580
Isn’t that a bit much?

252
00:28:04,368 --> 00:28:05,740
You think I’m joking?

253
00:28:06,454 --> 00:28:09,068
Believe it or not,

254
00:28:09,431 --> 00:28:10,734
that’s up to you.

255
00:28:12,485 --> 00:28:13,749
But don’t act like an idiot

256
00:28:13,774 --> 00:28:15,570
and get everyone else in trouble.

257
00:28:16,308 --> 00:28:17,443
You’ll bring us all down with you.

258
00:28:18,412 --> 00:28:20,197
Hey, enough!

259
00:28:20,927 --> 00:28:22,278
Are you going to fight in the store?

260
00:28:28,010 --> 00:28:29,260
Go take over the counter, too.

261
00:28:31,299 --> 00:28:32,680
He has no clue.

262
00:28:43,950 --> 00:28:44,846
I’ll do it myself.

263
00:29:28,274 --> 00:29:29,495
Hey, new guy!

264
00:29:30,434 --> 00:29:31,548
Take out the trash, too.

265
00:29:59,050 --> 00:29:59,883
Rule number nine.

266
00:30:00,707 --> 00:30:02,456
Employees must take the trash

267
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:04,717
to the bins behind the store every day at 3 am.

268
00:31:09,388 --> 00:31:10,184
Oh, hey.

269
00:31:10,704 --> 00:31:11,900
You just started here?

270
00:31:12,436 --> 00:31:14,053
Yeah, it’s my first day.

271
00:31:15,362 --> 00:31:17,084
Hello, I’m Good.

272
00:31:18,009 --> 00:31:18,660
I’m Metha.

273
00:31:19,374 --> 00:31:20,244
Metha.

274
00:31:23,092 --> 00:31:24,190
Ready to unload the delivery?

275
00:31:24,590 --> 00:31:25,945
Sure. I’ll help.

276
00:31:35,947 --> 00:31:36,827
Here, take this.

277
00:31:41,553 --> 00:31:44,342
They didn’t order much today. Just this one box.

278
00:31:46,693 --> 00:31:49,199
Check the delivery and sign for it, too.

279
00:31:49,974 --> 00:31:50,997
Rule number 11.

280
00:31:51,679 --> 00:31:53,456
Employees must receive and inspect deliveries

281
00:31:53,481 --> 00:31:55,398
from the delivery truck at the designated time.

282
00:31:57,191 --> 00:31:58,037
It’s rough, bro.

283
00:31:58,751 --> 00:31:59,975
We’re short-staffed.

284
00:32:00,332 --> 00:32:02,054
People keep quitting after just a little while.

285
00:32:03,158 --> 00:32:03,756
Why’s that?

286
00:32:05,054 --> 00:32:06,494
Because they break the rules.

287
00:32:09,264 --> 00:32:09,787
Break the rules?

288
00:32:11,423 --> 00:32:12,742
Haven’t you heard the stories?

289
00:32:14,112 --> 00:32:15,120
I heard

290
00:32:17,069 --> 00:32:19,781
there was once a night-shift employee

291
00:32:20,476 --> 00:32:21,686
working here.

292
00:32:22,422 --> 00:32:24,257
Welcome to Sunny Mart.

293
00:32:25,558 --> 00:32:26,769
And that night...

294
00:32:27,848 --> 00:32:28,978
an old man came in.

295
00:32:33,682 --> 00:32:34,840
What can I get for you, sir?

296
00:32:43,576 --> 00:32:45,028
Could you please speak up?

297
00:32:48,078 --> 00:32:50,244
Speak louder, old man. I can't hear you.

298
00:32:51,508 --> 00:32:52,758
Kid...

299
00:32:53,502 --> 00:32:54,390
Yes?

300
00:33:03,812 --> 00:33:05,232
You tricked me!

301
00:33:09,904 --> 00:33:10,685
Open the door!

302
00:33:39,546 --> 00:33:40,340
You know

303
00:33:41,060 --> 00:33:43,183
why that employee died?

304
00:33:45,257 --> 00:33:46,580
His name was Noom.

305
00:33:47,513 --> 00:33:49,348
And he answered when the customer called him.

306
00:33:49,839 --> 00:33:52,713
Whoa! You’re good!

307
00:33:53,346 --> 00:33:54,590
You’re smart!

308
00:33:56,804 --> 00:33:58,217
How did you know that?

309
00:33:58,318 --> 00:34:00,431
Honestly, you’re the first person

310
00:34:00,455 --> 00:34:03,257
who’s gotten it right on the first try.

311
00:34:03,891 --> 00:34:04,942
You’re a genius!

312
00:34:06,414 --> 00:34:07,198
Wait a second.

313
00:34:07,891 --> 00:34:09,144
This story’s true, right?

314
00:34:09,283 --> 00:34:10,179
No, it’s not.

315
00:34:12,678 --> 00:34:13,393
I’m kidding.

316
00:34:13,670 --> 00:34:14,620
I don’t know.

317
00:34:14,967 --> 00:34:16,646
That’s just what people say, so I’m passing it on.

318
00:34:18,952 --> 00:34:20,268
Just something to keep us awake,

319
00:34:20,292 --> 00:34:21,480
relax, and relieve some stress.

320
00:34:24,405 --> 00:34:26,047
Aren’t you scared working here, though?

321
00:34:26,371 --> 00:34:26,867
At night...

322
00:34:28,215 --> 00:34:29,407
have you seen anything weird?

323
00:34:39,740 --> 00:34:40,359
Hey!

324
00:34:41,729 --> 00:34:42,471
Hey!

325
00:34:42,982 --> 00:34:43,414
Huh?

326
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:45,457
Just messing with you, bro.

327
00:34:46,150 --> 00:34:47,718
Why so serious?

328
00:34:48,529 --> 00:34:50,012
Or have you actually seen something?

329
00:34:50,765 --> 00:34:51,389
Thank you.

330
00:34:54,443 --> 00:34:55,586
I better get back to work.

331
00:34:55,773 --> 00:34:57,170
All right, bro. See you.

332
00:35:00,148 --> 00:35:01,482
Hope you stick around for a long time.

333
00:35:02,916 --> 00:35:04,452
I’m tired of getting to know new people.

334
00:35:04,729 --> 00:35:06,485
This store goes through staff like crazy.

335
00:35:06,509 --> 00:35:07,876
I barely get to know anyone before they’re gone.

336
00:35:08,993 --> 00:35:09,851
Hang in there, bro.

337
00:35:37,855 --> 00:35:40,537
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

338
